Select the PubChem candidate that best matches the identity expressed by
the user request.

User request: "{{ query }}"
Formula: {{ formula }}
{% if search_name %}Search name: {{ search_name }}{% endif %}

Formula-filtered PubChem candidates:
{% for c in candidates %}
[{{ c.index }}] CID {{ c.cid }}: {{ c.name }}
  Formula: {{ c.formula }}
  SMILES: {{ c.get("isomeric_smiles") or c.get("smiles") or "N/A" }}
  {% if c.get("inchi_key") %}InChIKey: {{ c.get("inchi_key") }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

Decision rules:
- decision="select": one candidate matches the identity expressed by the original
  request.
{% if minimal_interaction %}
- decision="not_found": the request specifies an identity or stereochemistry but no
  candidate matches it.
- When at least one plausible candidate exists, always return decision="select".
  Do not return ambiguous.
{% else %}
- decision="ambiguous": multiple chemically distinct candidates remain plausible
  and the request does not distinguish them.
- decision="not_found": the request specifies an identity or stereochemistry but no
  candidate matches it.
{% endif %}

Selection rules:
- Apply evidence in this order: explicit information in the original request;
  candidate names and stereochemistry-preserving identifiers (SMILES, InChIKey);
  extracted search name.
- Require the requested connectivity. Formula agreement alone is insufficient.
- Positional and constitutional isomers are distinct. Enantiomers, diastereomers,
  and E/Z isomers are distinct when stereochemistry is specified. Correct
  connectivity with wrong handedness is then incorrect.
{% if minimal_interaction %}
- When plausible candidates differ in unspecified stereochemistry, tautomer, or
  protonation state: select when the name has one well-established meaning in common
  usage (e.g. "glucose" = D-glucose, "adrenaline" = L-adrenaline).
- When multiple plausible candidates remain after applying the evidence above:
  select the most defensible candidate, or the lower-index candidate when equally
  defensible; set needs_review=true; state the assumption in selection_reason; and
  list alternative candidates in suggested_candidates.
- When one candidate clearly matches the requested identity, select with
  needs_review=false.
{% else %}
- If plausible candidates differ only in unspecified stereochemistry, tautomer, or
  protonation state, return ambiguous — unless the exact requested name has one
  well-established meaning in common usage. A name that unambiguously designates
  one stereoisomer (e.g. "glucose" = D-glucose, "adrenaline" = L-adrenaline) may
  be selected; document the reasoning in selection_reason.
{% endif %}
{% if minimal_interaction %}
- For select: provide a valid selected_index. Use suggested_candidates=[] when
  needs_review=false; when needs_review=true, list up to five alternative plausible
  candidates in suggested_candidates. Set user_message=null.
- For not_found: use selected_index=null, needs_review=false, and explain what the
  user should specify next in one concise user_message.
- Always provide selection_reason: decisive evidence for unambiguous select, the
  assumption made when needs_review=true, or why no candidate matches for not_found.
- Set needs_review=true whenever the selection rests on an unresolved assumption
  (stereochemistry, tautomer, protonation, etc.). needs_review does not indicate
  failure.
{% else %}
- For select, provide a valid selected_index and suggested_candidates=[]. For
  ambiguous or not_found, use selected_index=null and explain what the user should
  specify next in one concise, flowing user_message.
- Always provide selection_reason. It should briefly state the
  decisive evidence for select, or the unresolved distinction for ambiguous or
  not_found.
- For ambiguity, offer up to five chemically distinct choices from the supplied
  candidates. Each suggestion must use an actual candidate index and preserve the
  distinguishing name or stereochemical qualifier. Suggestions are not exhaustive.
{% endif %}
- Set confidence to reflect how certain you are about the selection (1=low, 5=high). Use confidence=5 only when the identity is unambiguous.

Return one JSON object and nothing else:

{
  "decision": "<select{% if not minimal_interaction %} | ambiguous{% endif %} | not_found>",
  "selected_index": <integer candidate index or null>,
  "user_message": "<selection explanation or clarification guidance, or null if select>",
  "selection_reason": "<brief audit reason for the decision>",
  "suggested_candidates": [
    {
      "index": <integer candidate index>,
      "suggested_query": "<specific follow-up request>"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": <integer 1 to 5>,
  "needs_review": <true | false>
}

Important: always output a complete, closed JSON object before stopping.
